# v0.9.1 Phase 8 Task 32 — Lobby.lobbies as the wall target list.
#
# Spec §9.1 / §14 exit-criterion 5: A's `wall "hi"` reaches B/C/D but
# not A.  The wall body (in lobby.u) iterates Lobby.lobbies skipping
# `this`.  This fixture verifies the substrate: Lobby.lobbies contains
# exactly one entry per active session (the session realm's global
# object), and that List indexing returns a non-nil lobby reference.
#
# The cross-session broadcast aspect (A's wall actually reaching B/C/D
# via per-realm writer routing) is verified end-to-end by
# tests/unit/test_repl_multi_client.c (Task 33) over real TCP loopback.
# The Lobby.wall closure body calls l.echo(msg, tag, "***") which now
# works end-to-end via the v0.10.11 W4 fix (Lobby.echo uses
# this.__builtin_lobby_send, resolving through the proto chain).
# The bare-name auto-walk root-cause remains a v1.x emit follow-up.

